################################################################################
# 15C + d  --  D2 active target at 300 torr, room temperature
#
# NEW FILE for the C15d workspace (macro/Unpack_HDF5/C15d/). Nothing else reads it.
#
# * THE DRIFT WORKING POINT. Two EXTERNAL facts fix it, because this data cannot:
#     sampling 3.125 MHz (320 ns/TB)   -- confirmed from the DAQ
#     beam energy ~190 MeV             -- run log
# Together they force dv = 0.556 cm/us: 1000 mm / (320 ns * 0.556 cm/us) = 562 time buckets, and
# the 15C(d,d) elastic ridge then returns ~192 MeV. Pad plane at TB 20, so the entrance is 582.
#
# * TBEntrance 582 IS BEYOND THE 512-SAMPLE RECORD, ON PURPOSE. The window is never sampled: the
# drift takes 562 buckets and the DAQ stores 512, so charge from the far end arrives after the
# record closes. That is why the latest-arriving charge per track SPIKES ~8x against the record end
# and stops -- DAQ truncation, not the chamber. Any window TB read off this data is therefore a
# LOWER bound, mm/TB an UPPER bound, and a ridge beam energy a LOWER bound. Taking the apparent
# edge at face value gave dv 1.307 and 163 MeV; it is an artifact.
#
# * WHAT WAS TRIED AND IS EXCLUDED, at 320 ns and a 1000 mm chamber:
#     dv 1.136 (Spyral's implied value) -> 3.635 mm/TB -> 275 TB -> ridge gives  88 MeV
#     dv 0.653 (apparent record edge)   -> 2.090 mm/TB -> 479 TB -> ridge gives 161 MeV
#     dv 0.556 (ADOPTED)                -> 1.779 mm/TB -> 562 TB -> ridge gives 192 MeV
# Spyral has NO drift velocity at all: its z is (window_tb - tb)/(window_tb - mm_tb) * length, so
# its 300/25 anchors imply 3.635 mm/TB, the first row above.
#
# * OPEN QUESTION worth revisiting: 0.556 cm/us is LOW. a2091 uses 1.30 for H2 at the same 300 torr
# and 45 kV/m, and H2/D2 electron transport is nearly identical. So either the field for these runs
# was not 45 kV/m, or the 1000 mm drift length is wrong, or dv really is this low. The working
# point is consistent with the two external facts either way, but the gas physics is not yet.
#
# * KEEP THIS BLOCK ABOVE [AtDigiPar]. A standalone comment line INSIDE the section makes
# FairParAsciiFileIo stop parsing there and everything after it reads as zero, silently.
#
# Density matches geometry/media.geo entry TargetD2_300 (6.5643e-5 g/cm3) EXACTLY, so
# the UKF's CATIMA model and genfit's TGeo material describe the same gas. Do not edit
# one without the other.
################################################################################
[AtDigiPar]
PadPlaneX:Int_t                864   # mm
PadPlaneZ:Int_t               1344   # mm
PadSizeX:Int_t                   8   # mm
PadSizeZ:Int_t                  12   # mm
PadRows:Int_t                  108   #
PadLayers:Int_t                112   #
AnodeWirePlaneY:Double_t     -4.05   # mm
GroundWirePlaneY:Double_t     -8.1   # mm
GatingWirePlaneY:Double_t      -14   # mm
EField:Double_t              45000   # V/m   (Spyral electric_field)
NumTbs:Int_t                   512
SamplingRate:Int_t               3   # -> 320 ns/TB = 3.125 MHz, CONFIRMED from the DAQ
DriftVelocity:Double_t       0.556   # cm/us  set by 3.125 MHz + Ebeam ~190; see header
DriftLength:Double_t        1000.0   # mm
YDivider:Int_t                1000   # Full drift length divided by this when finding clusters
GasFile:Int_t                    2
PadPlaneFile:Int_t               3
PadShapeFile:Int_t               4
BField:Double_t               2.85   # Tesla  (sign is a FITTER argument, not a par entry)
TiltAng:Double_t               0.0   # Degrees
TB0:Int_t                       20   # pad-plane TB, MEASURED; DEPRECATED and IGNORED anyway
LorentzAngle:Double_t          0.0   # Lorentz Angle
TBEntrance:Int_t               582   # = TB0 + 562; BEYOND the 512 record, never sampled
ZPadPlane:Double_t          1000.0   # mm  Spyral detector_length
Density:Double_t           0.065643  # mg/cm3 == 6.5643e-5 g/cm3. D2, 300 torr, ~295.2 K (22 C) --
ThetaPad:Double_t            110.9   # AT-TPC pad plane rotation
ThetaRot:Double_t              0.0   # Second Lorentz Angle
GasPressure:Double_t           300   # torr
EIonize:Double_t            15.603   # eV
Fano:Double_t                 0.24   #
CoefL:Double_t              0.0009   # Longitudinal diffusion [cm^2/us]
CoefT:Double_t              0.0009   # Transverse diffusion [cm^2/us]
Gain:Double_t                10000   # Micromegas gain
GETGain:Double_t              1000   # GET electronics gain [fC]
PeakingTime:Int_t              720   # ns
MaxRange:Double_t            500.0   # mm
